    "disposition": "downgrade",
    "reason": "The 5.16× price gap on leaf-matched 60/80-leaf books persists after CPI adjustment, but several legitimate cost drivers remain unresolved: (1) Federal contracts explicitly include distribution to dispersed schools across constituencies/LGAs (titles mention \"SUPPLY AND DISTRIBUTION\" or \"PRINTING AND SUPPLY\"), while Oyo contracts are titled \"procurement\" with no stated delivery scope. (2) Federal lot sizes are 8k–74k vs Oyo's 200k+, giving Oyo massive economies of scale. (3) Federal contracts span 2023–2024 vs Oyo 2022 only; specification upgrades (cover weight, paper GSM, colour, customization level) are not captured in leaf count alone. (4) Geographic dispersion and last-mile delivery to selected schools in specific wards/constituencies add cost. Without detailed spec sheets or a breakdown of production vs distribution, the gap cannot be attributed to overpricing."
  },
  {
    "leadId": "twin-award-ocds-gyl66f-539001003-002244/17018-ocds-gyl66f-539001003-002381/15613",
    "disposition": "downgrade",
    "reason": "The two federal contracts share the same date (2024-10-15) and quantity (8,200) but target different school clusters (Tudun/S vs Galadimawa II). The near-identical values (0.327% difference) are consistent with separate lots for distinct geographic areas under the same specification, rather than duplicate releases."
  }
]

